@startuml sd_us209
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US209 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "ATCC" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of airports-routes" as EAR
box "airports-routes-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "AirportController" as AirportController
participant "ViewAirportRoutesUseCase" as ViewAirportRoutesUseCase
database "own database" as DBAR
end box
collections "peer replicas\nairports-routes-m" as PAR
== GET /api/airports/{iataCode}/routes ==
Actor -> EAR : GET /api/airports/{iataCode}/routes\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EAR -> AirportController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
AirportController -> ViewAirportRoutesUseCase : execute(...)
ViewAirportRoutesUseCase -> DBAR : own routes
ViewAirportRoutesUseCase -> PAR : GET /internal/replicas/routes\n(every peer in parallel)
PAR --> ViewAirportRoutesUseCase : their routes
ViewAirportRoutesUseCase -> DBAR : airports (catalog, complete here)
ViewAirportRoutesUseCase -> ViewAirportRoutesUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
ViewAirportRoutesUseCase --> AirportController : result
AirportController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
